# Spanish A1 — beginner vocabulary
# Format: word | translations (semicolon-separated) | example sentence | category | difficulty (1-5)

# Greetings and courtesy
hola | hello; hi | ¡Hola! ¿Cómo estás? | greetings | 1 | Hi! How are you?
buenos días | good morning | Buenos días, señora Gómez. | greetings | 1 | Good morning, Mrs. Gómez.
buenas tardes | good afternoon | Buenas tardes, ¿en qué puedo ayudarle? | greetings | 1 | Good afternoon, how can I help you?
buenas noches | good evening; good night | Buenas noches, hasta mañana. | greetings | 1 | Good night, see you tomorrow.
adiós | goodbye; bye | Adiós, nos vemos el lunes. | greetings | 1 | Goodbye, see you on Monday.
hasta luego | see you later | Hasta luego, tengo prisa. | greetings | 1 | See you later, I'm in a hurry.
gracias | thank you; thanks | Muchas gracias por tu ayuda. | greetings | 1 | Thank you very much for your help.
de nada | you're welcome | De nada, ha sido un placer. | greetings | 1 | You're welcome, it was a pleasure.
por favor | please | Un café, por favor. | greetings | 1 | A coffee, please.
perdón | sorry; excuse me | Perdón, no te había visto. | greetings | 1 | Sorry, I didn't see you.
disculpe | excuse me (formal) | Disculpe, ¿dónde está el baño? | greetings | 2 | Excuse me, where is the bathroom?
mucho gusto | nice to meet you | Mucho gusto, soy Marta. | greetings | 2 | Nice to meet you, I'm Marta.
bienvenido | welcome | ¡Bienvenido a Madrid! | greetings | 2 | Welcome to Madrid!

# Basics
sí | yes | Sí, entiendo perfectamente. | basics | 1 | Yes, I understand perfectly.
no | no | No, gracias. | basics | 1 | No, thank you.
quizás | maybe; perhaps | Quizás vayamos a la playa. | basics | 2 | Maybe we'll go to the beach.
muy | very | Estoy muy cansado hoy. | basics | 1 | I'm very tired today.
mucho | a lot; much | Trabajo mucho los lunes. | basics | 1 | I work a lot on Mondays.
poco | little; not much | Hablo poco español todavía. | basics | 1 | I don't speak much Spanish yet.
también | also; too | Yo también quiero ir. | basics | 1 | I want to go too.
pero | but | Quiero salir, pero está lloviendo. | basics | 1 | I want to go out, but it's raining.
porque | because | No fui porque estaba enfermo. | basics | 1 | I didn't go because I was sick.
cómo | how | ¿Cómo se dice esto en español? | basics | 1 | How do you say this in Spanish?
dónde | where | ¿Dónde vives? | basics | 1 | Where do you live?
cuándo | when | ¿Cuándo llega el tren? | basics | 1 | When does the train arrive?
quién | who | ¿Quién es esa chica? | basics | 1 | Who is that girl?
qué | what | ¿Qué haces esta noche? | basics | 1 | What are you doing tonight?
cuánto | how much; how many | ¿Cuánto cuesta esto? | basics | 1 | How much does this cost?
bien | well; fine | Estoy bien, gracias. | basics | 1 | I'm fine, thanks.
mal | badly; bad | Hoy me siento mal. | basics | 1 | I feel bad today.
siempre | always | Siempre tomo café por la mañana. | basics | 2 | I always have coffee in the morning.
nunca | never | Nunca he estado en Sevilla. | basics | 2 | I've never been to Seville.
ahora | now | Ahora tengo que irme. | basics | 2 | I have to go now.
aquí | here | El restaurante está aquí cerca. | basics | 1 | The restaurant is near here.

# Numbers
uno | one | Solo tengo uno. | numbers | 1 | I only have one.
dos | two | Quiero dos billetes. | numbers | 1 | I want two tickets.
tres | three | Hay tres libros en la mesa. | numbers | 1 | There are three books on the table.
cuatro | four | La reunión es a las cuatro. | numbers | 1 | The meeting is at four.
cinco | five | Vivo en el piso cinco. | numbers | 1 | I live on the fifth floor.
seis | six | Me levanto a las seis. | numbers | 1 | I get up at six.
siete | seven | La semana tiene siete días. | numbers | 1 | A week has seven days.
ocho | eight | La tienda abre a las ocho. | numbers | 1 | The shop opens at eight.
nueve | nine | Tengo nueve primos. | numbers | 1 | I have nine cousins.
diez | ten | Cuesta diez euros. | numbers | 1 | It costs ten euros.
veinte | twenty | Tengo veinte minutos de pausa. | numbers | 2 | I have a twenty-minute break.
cien | hundred | El libro tiene cien páginas. | numbers | 2 | The book has a hundred pages.
mil | thousand | La ciudad tiene mil años de historia. | numbers | 2 | The city has a thousand years of history.
primero | first | Es mi primer día de trabajo. | numbers | 2 | It's my first day at work.

# Family and people
familia | family | Mi familia es muy grande. | family | 1 | My family is very big.
madre | mother | Mi madre cocina muy bien. | family | 1 | My mother cooks very well.
padre | father | Mi padre trabaja en un banco. | family | 1 | My father works at a bank.
hijo | son; child | Su hijo tiene cinco años. | family | 1 | Her son is five years old.
hija | daughter | Su hija estudia medicina. | family | 1 | His daughter is studying medicine.
hermano | brother | Tengo un hermano mayor. | family | 1 | I have an older brother.
hermana | sister | Mi hermana vive en Barcelona. | family | 1 | My sister lives in Barcelona.
abuelo | grandfather | Mi abuelo cuenta buenas historias. | family | 2 | My grandfather tells good stories.
abuela | grandmother | La abuela hace una tortilla estupenda. | family | 2 | Grandma makes a wonderful tortilla.
esposo | husband | Su esposo es profesor. | family | 2 | Her husband is a teacher.
esposa | wife | Mi esposa adora viajar. | family | 2 | My wife loves to travel.
amigo | friend | Voy al cine con un amigo. | family | 1 | I'm going to the movies with a friend.
niño | child; little boy | El niño juega en el parque. | family | 1 | The boy is playing in the park.
chica | girl | Esa chica es mi vecina. | family | 1 | That girl is my neighbor.
hombre | man | Ese hombre trabaja aquí hace años. | family | 1 | That man has worked here for years.
mujer | woman; wife | La mujer de la caja es muy amable. | family | 1 | The woman at the checkout is very nice.

# Food and drink
agua | water | Quiero un vaso de agua. | food | 1 | I want a glass of water.
pan | bread | Compro pan todas las mañanas. | food | 1 | I buy bread every morning.
vino | wine | Una copa de vino tinto, por favor. | food | 1 | A glass of red wine, please.
café | coffee | Tomo un café en el bar. | food | 1 | I have a coffee at the café.
leche | milk | Bebo leche en el desayuno. | food | 1 | I drink milk at breakfast.
arroz | rice | El arroz está listo. | food | 2 | The rice is ready.
carne | meat | No como carne los viernes. | food | 2 | I don't eat meat on Fridays.
pescado | fish (food) | El pescado está fresquísimo hoy. | food | 2 | The fish is really fresh today.
queso | cheese | Este queso es manchego. | food | 2 | This cheese is Manchego.
fruta | fruit | Como fruta todos los días. | food | 2 | I eat fruit every day.
verdura | vegetables | Compro verdura en el mercado. | food | 2 | I buy vegetables at the market.
huevo | egg | Quiero dos huevos fritos. | food | 2 | I want two fried eggs.
azúcar | sugar | ¿Tomas azúcar en el café? | food | 2 | Do you take sugar in your coffee?
sal | salt | Le falta un poco de sal. | food | 2 | It needs a little salt.
desayuno | breakfast | El desayuno es a las siete. | food | 2 | Breakfast is at seven.
almuerzo | lunch | El almuerzo es a las dos. | food | 2 | Lunch is at two.
cena | dinner | La cena ya está lista. | food | 2 | Dinner is ready.
restaurante | restaurant | Conozco un buen restaurante aquí. | food | 2 | I know a good restaurant around here.

# Time
día | day | ¿Qué día es hoy? | time | 1 | What day is it today?
semana | week | Nos vemos la próxima semana. | time | 2 | See you next week.
mes | month | Me voy el mes que viene. | time | 2 | I'm leaving next month.
año | year | Estudio español desde hace un año. | time | 1 | I've been studying Spanish for a year.
hoy | today | Hoy hace mucho calor. | time | 1 | It's very hot today.
mañana | tomorrow; morning | Mañana tengo un examen. | time | 1 | I have an exam tomorrow.
ayer | yesterday | Ayer fui al museo. | time | 1 | Yesterday I went to the museum.
tarde | afternoon; late | Por la tarde estudio. | time | 2 | I study in the afternoon.
noche | night | Anoche dormí mal. | time | 2 | I slept badly last night.
hora | hour; time | ¿Qué hora es? | time | 1 | What time is it?
minuto | minute | Espera un minuto, por favor. | time | 2 | Wait a minute, please.
lunes | Monday | El lunes vuelvo al trabajo. | time | 2 | On Monday I go back to work.
sábado | Saturday | El sábado vamos a la montaña. | time | 2 | On Saturday we're going to the mountains.
domingo | Sunday | Los domingos duermo hasta tarde. | time | 2 | On Sundays I sleep late.

# Places and travel
casa | house; home | Vuelvo a casa a las seis. | housing | 1 | I go back home at six.
ciudad | city | Madrid es una ciudad preciosa. | travel | 1 | Madrid is a beautiful city.
calle | street | La calle está cortada por obras. | travel | 2 | The street is closed for roadworks.
estación | station | La estación está a diez minutos. | transportation | 2 | The station is ten minutes away.
tren | train | El tren a Valencia sale a las nueve. | transportation | 2 | The train to Valencia leaves at nine.
autobús | bus | Cojo el autobús número veinte. | transportation | 2 | I take the number twenty bus.
coche | car | El coche está aparcado detrás. | transportation | 2 | The car is parked around the back.
aeropuerto | airport | Llego al aeropuerto a las ocho. | transportation | 2 | I get to the airport at eight.
hotel | hotel | Hemos reservado un hotel céntrico. | travel | 2 | We've booked a hotel in the city center.
tienda | shop; store | La tienda cierra a las siete. | shopping | 2 | The shop closes at seven.
mercado | market | El mercado abre los sábados. | shopping | 2 | The market opens on Saturdays.
billete | ticket | Compré el billete por internet. | travel | 2 | I bought the ticket online.

# Everyday things and adjectives
libro | book | Estoy leyendo un libro en español. | education | 1 | I'm reading a book in Spanish.
trabajo | work; job | Me gusta mucho mi trabajo. | work | 1 | I really like my job.
escuela | school | Los niños van a la escuela a las ocho. | education | 1 | The children go to school at eight.
dinero | money | No llevo dinero encima. | shopping | 2 | I don't have any money on me.
teléfono | telephone | Te llamo por teléfono esta noche. | technology | 1 | I'll phone you tonight.
grande | big; large | Vivo en una casa grande. | basics | 1 | I live in a big house.
pequeño | small; little | Tengo un piso pequeño. | basics | 1 | I have a small apartment.
nuevo | new | Me compré un ordenador nuevo. | basics | 1 | I bought a new computer.
bonito | pretty; nice | ¡Qué día tan bonito! | basics | 1 | What a beautiful day!
bueno | good | Este café está muy bueno. | basics | 1 | This coffee is really good.
calor | heat; hot | Hoy hace calor. | weather | 1 | It's hot today.
frío | cold | En invierno hace frío aquí. | weather | 1 | It's cold here in winter.
lluvia | rain | La lluvia empezó al amanecer. | weather | 2 | The rain started at dawn.
sol | sun | Hoy hace sol. | weather | 1 | It's sunny today.
feliz | happy | Estoy feliz de verte. | emotions | 2 | I'm happy to see you.
cansado | tired | Estoy cansado después del trabajo. | emotions | 2 | I'm tired after work.
